L846) | `slot >= 0` (re-find of the moved-in key) | unreachable for a consistent table |\n| A6 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (L849) | `b->index[i] == final_index` | unreachable for a consistent table |\n| A7 | `stbds_stralloc` (L913) | `len <= a->remaining` after block allocation | unreachable via the public path (only with a hand-forged arena, which segfaults in both implementations on the next line) |\n| A8 | `arr_ins` (L953) | `arr[i] == num` right after `arrins` | unreachable: `arrins` writes `num` at `i` |\n| A9 | `arr_ins` (L955) | `arr[4] == 4` for `i < 4` | unreachable: inserting at `i<4` into `[1,2,3,4]` always leaves `4` at index 4 |\n| A10 | file scope (L495) | `sizeof(size_t) == 8` (compile-time `typedef` trick) | mirrored by `const _: () = assert!(size_of::<usize>() == 8)` in Rust |\n\nBecause A1–A9 are unreachable through the exported API with a self-consistent\ndata structure, the Rust side keeps them as `debug_assert!` without any\nobservable behavioural difference; A10 is a hard compile-time assertion in both.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1380,"cache_read_input_tokens":63384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1380,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4447cbe5-415d-478b-a6fb-8cbc8eb01e60","uuid":"bd1ae386-cd76-4d5c-8cd4-7a6d2f384b95","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:00:44.212Z"}
