{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7ov5jblmhvs4fvll74lqmqn4pn6r4ukjz3xnxezpkl4qs2whaola","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — 80 differential tests pass, 1 real translation bug found and fixed.**\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n`translation/src/lib.rs` used `debug_assert!` for all 8 mirrored `STBDS_ASSERT`s. The C library is compiled **without `NDEBUG`**, so its `assert()`s are live. This is observable: deleting a non-last element with `mode == STBDS_HM_PTR_TO_STRING` (2) makes `stbds_hmdel_key`'s key re-find take the binary comparator on a `char*` field, so `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0)` fires. C → `SIGABRT`; Rust → assert compiled out, then indexed `storage[-1 >> 3]` and corrupted memory. Converted all 8 to `assert!` (with `panic = \"abort\"` this aborts exactly like C). Subprocess test now shows 134 vs 134.\n\n## Artifacts (crate root)\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 16 C dynamic symbols; Rust `.so` exports every one, diff empty, no non-libc undefined symbols. Nothing was missing, so no C source needed translating.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 38 rejection rows + 10 `STBDS_ASSERT` rows, each mapped to a passing test. Includes reachability analysis per assert.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 40 configuration rows (mode classes incl. out-of-enum, all 4 `string.mode`s, elemsize/keysize/keyoffset shapes, bucket/growth/shrink/tombstone thresholds, arena block growth), all `[x]`.\n\n## Tests (`translation/tests/`, all via `libloading` on both `.so`s)\n`common/mod.rs` harness snapshots the *entire* structure after every operation — array header, all payload bytes (pointer words blanked, strings compared by content), every `stbds_hash_index` scalar, and every `hash[8]`/`index[8]` bucket entry — with fixed-seed randomized inputs.\n\n- `phase_b_lowlevel.rs` (15) — `arrgrowf`/`arrfreef`, `hash_bytes` (all `len%8` tail cases + high-bit sign-extension), `hash_string`, seed advance, `stralloc`/`strreset` (block growth to saturation), `strkey`, `arr_ins`.\n- `phase_b_map.rs` (26) — rows 10–32, 39, 40.\n- `phase_c_errors.rs` (36 + 1 helper) — one test per `ERRORS.md` row, plus NULL/zero-length/oversized/out-of-range-enum boundaries. Three crashing UB paths compared in subprocesses by exit signal.\n- `symbols.rs` (3) — `nm -D` parity.\n\n`./verify.sh` rebuilds both libraries, diffs symbols, and runs everything across all feature combos (Cargo.toml has no `[features]`, so one configuration). No binary/driver exists in either tree, so no stdout comparison applies.\n\nTwo notes: `cargo` needs `--offline` here (crates.io is proxy-blocked; `libloading 0.8.9` was already cached), and a *debug*-profile `.so` diverges on one row only — rustc's debug-only null-check turns the C's post-`realloc`-failure UB into an abort instead of `SIGSEGV`. Documented in `ERRORS.md`; the release cdylib (the counterpart artifact) matches."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":826,"cache_read_input_tokens":198028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":826,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4447cbe5-415d-478b-a6fb-8cbc8eb01e60","uuid":"feab5965-c89f-476a-b344-45f90fbf9080","timestamp":"2026-09-05T06:17:33.100Z"}
